{"id": "EUVD-2026-74619", "enisaUuid": "24074d85-dbad-377e-bce3-03db3580e5e8", "description": "An issue was discovered in the mirage-crypto-ec function before 2.2.0 for OCaml. The ECDSA functions {P256,P384,P521}.Dsa.pub_of_octets accept 0x00, the encoding of the point at infinity, as a public key. With that public key, signatures can be forged without a private key.", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T04:08:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-09T13:02:51", "baseScore": 6.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-13"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v5p-5xxr-9xf8", "CVE-2026-87733"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ea6ea005-68e3-3e65-999e-9d5b6d5d579d", "product": {"name": "mirage-crypto-ec", "vendor": {"name": "OCaml"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5f26b690-6253-39ab-9121-5c4d566c18e0", "vendor": {"name": "OCaml"}}], "isExploited": false}